                <invention-title lang="de">SIMULATIONEN KONDENSIERTER MATERIEN AUF QUANTENCOMPUTERN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">SIMULATIONS DE MATIÈRES CONDENSÉES SUR DES ORDINATEURS QUANTIQUES</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">CONDENSED MATTER SIMULATIONS ON QUANTUM COMPUTERS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method of simulating fermionic systems includes receiving a list of interactions between fermionic modes and determining an interactivity graph. Vertices of the interactivity graph are uniquely associated with the modes, and edges of the interactivity graph connect every pair of vertices whose associated pair of modes interact. Next, disjoint clusters of modes are identified and pairs of connected clusters from a set of pairs of candidate connected clusters are selected.. Each of the edge and vertex operators is implemented as a qubit operators on a quantum computer while preserving commutation and anticommutation relationships. Finally at least one fermionic interaction is simulated on the quantum computer by enacting unitary qubit operations. The disclosure also relates to computer programs and computer systems for enacting the method.</p>
            </abstract>
